# Per-machine configuration. Copy to .env and edit -- .env is gitignored, this
# file is committed.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything here is a plain environment variable, which is the whole point:
# NLA/src/config.py is already fully env-overridable, and POLARIS already reads
# polaris_poc/.env, so this adds a place to put values rather than a new
# mechanism. Anything exported in your shell takes precedence over this file.
#
# Only set what differs from the defaults -- an empty .env is valid.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- NLA side
# (start_nla.sh -- the machine with the GPU)

# Target model T. Must be the model the AV/AR pair was trained on, not merely
# the same family: the public 7B pair is fine-tuned from the *Instruct* model,
# and base activations would decode to confident nonsense.
#NLA_MODEL_ID=Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct

# cuda | cuda:1 | cpu | auto.  'auto' shards across every visible GPU, which is
# what the 7B AV+AR pair (26 GB) needs on 2x 24 GB cards.
#NLA_DEVICE=auto

# auto | bfloat16 | float16 | float32.  'auto' picks bf16 where supported.
#NLA_DTYPE=auto

# NOT set here on purpose: NLA_PROBE_LAYER. The layer is a property of the
# released checkpoint pair, not of this machine, so it belongs in PROBE_LAYERS
# in NLA/src/config.py where a wrong value gets reviewed. Setting it here would
# let it drift silently per host.

# Where activation traces are written. Worth pointing at a disk you actually
# monitor: at 7B (d_model 3584, float16) a trace costs ~5.6 KB per token, so a
# ~1.5k-token POLARIS reasoning step is ~8 MB and 1000 of them are ~8 GB.
#NLA_TRACE_DIR=/path/with/room/traces

# Groups one run's traces into a subdirectory. Blank -> timestamped per start.
#NLA_RUN_ID=

# Set to 0 to disable trace capture entirely (serves the model, writes nothing).
#NLA_CAPTURE=1

# Listen address and port. Keep the bind on loopback when reaching this box by
# SSH tunnel -- there is no auth on this endpoint.
#NLA_PORT=8000
#NLA_BIND=127.0.0.1

# Generation cap per LLM call.
#NLA_MAX_NEW_TOKENS=256

# Seconds to wait for T + AV + AR to load. 7B from a cold HF cache is minutes.
#NLA_WAIT_MODEL=600

# Where this server finds POLARIS's dashboard bridge. With `ssh -R 8090:...`
# from the POLARIS box, the default already points down the tunnel.
#POLARIS_BRIDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8090

# ------------------------------------------------------------ POLARIS side
# (start_polaris.sh -- the machine with Docker + tmux)

# OpenAI-compatible endpoint the reasoner calls. With `ssh -L 8000:...` to the
# GPU box, the default already points up the tunnel.
#NLA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1

# Model name sent to that endpoint. The NLA server ignores it (it serves
# whatever NLA_MODEL_ID it loaded); it only shows up in logs and traces.
#NLA_MODEL_NAME=local-nla

# Dashboard bridge port. Must match the -R port in the SSH tunnel.
#BRIDGE_PORT=8090

# Required by POLARIS whenever --llm-provider openai_compatible is used, even
# though a local NLA server never checks it.
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=local
